' bug-57: a `WHILE` condition that folds a loop-mutated local through a string
' folder (`toString`) used the local's stale loop-entry constant, frozen in the
' single emitted comparison above the back edge, so the loop never observed `c`
' changing and ran forever.
'
' The body's guard bounds the iteration count and exits with a distinct marker,
' so a buggy binary produces a well-formed WRONG result (exit 0) rather than
' hanging: on the buggy codegen the frozen `toString(0) <> "3"` stays true, the
' guard fires, and it prints "looping c=21".
IMPORT io

FUNC main AS Integer
  MUT c AS Integer = 0
  MUT guard AS Integer = 0
  WHILE toString(c) <> "3"
    c = c + 1
    guard = guard + 1
    IF guard > 20 THEN
      io::print("looping c=" & toString(c))
      RETURN 0
    END IF
  END WHILE
  io::print("terminated c=" & toString(c))
  RETURN 0
END FUNC
